---
alwaysApply: true
---

To create a new worktree with a working environment use the script `npm run wt:create <branch-name>`

Extension repos under `extensions/` and `extensions/plugins/` are cloned automatically from your current checkout (no repo list in git). Use `WT_SKIP_EXTENSIONS=1` to skip.

The optional MCP server repo is cloned into `platform/mcp` the same way when present in your checkout. Use `WT_SKIP_MCP=1` to skip. See `platform/MCP.md`.

Always create worktrees from the `dev` branch, if the working folder is not on `dev` use `npm run wt:create <branch-name> dev`

If you need to create a workspace on an existing branch use `npm run wt:create <branch-name> --existing`
